      "content": "that makes sense, but i'm also wondering about the specific descriptions. like, it uses a lot of words to describe the native people as being almost like part of the landscape or just \"wild\" and \"primitive\" noises. if i'm writing for a post-colonial class, wouldn't it be a bit of a stretch to just say \"it was the time period\"? like, isn't there a difference between reflecting the era and actually using those tropes to justify describing people that way? how much weight should i give to the idea that the book itself might be inherently biased vs just showing the bias of the characters?",
